      "extract": "Chiral perturbation theory ($\\chi$PT for short) is regarded nowadays as the effective field theory dual to QCD at very low energies. It describes the dynamics of the pseudo--Goldstone bosons ($\\pi,\\, K,\\,\\eta$) in an expansion in powers of external momenta and masses. It incorporates the assumed QCD symmetries such as parity, charge conjugation and, most important, the spontaneous breakdown of chiral symmetry. The",
      "extractCut": true
    },
