        },
        {
          "term": "bar",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "The external field method was first introduced by Leutwyler [@Leut], and makes easier the computation of QCD Green functions and form factors. It enforces chiral Ward identities exactly by promoting the global chiral symmetry to a local one. The basic idea is to introduce in the QCD action a set of local fields coupled to the QCD currents : $$\\!Z[v_{\\mu},a_{\\mu},s,p,{\\bar{t}}_{\\,\\mu\\nu}]=\\!\\!\\int\\!",
      "extractCut": true
    },
