        }
      ],
      "extract": "$\\chi$PT is based on the spontaneous breakdown of the global $G=SU(n_f)_L\\otimes SU(n_f)_R$ flavour symmetry down to its subgroup $SU(n_f)_V$. The dynamical fields $\\phi^a=(\\pi,K,\\eta)$ are assumed to be the (pseudo--)Goldstone bosons associated to this breakdown. The general formalism for effective Lagrangians with spontaneously broken symmetries was worked out by Callan, Coleman, Wess and Zumino [@CWZ], and for",
      "extractCut": true
    },
