      "extract": "The number of operators entering in the chiral Lagrangian is of course not restricted by symmetry. So in principle there are an infinite number of them, each one multiplied by an unknown coefficient (this is in agreement with the fact that $\\chi$PT is not normalizable *stricto sensu*). So if one has to take them all into account in any calculation, loses all predictive power. At low energies (compared with the",
      "extractCut": true
